<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samnite Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">343–290 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Samnite Wars were three wars fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> and the Samnites of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a> between 343 and 290 BCE. Despite defeats such as the Caudine Forks in 321 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> prevailed and, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sentinum">Battle of Sentinum</a> in 295 BCE, became the dominant power in central and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Neighbouring peoples who sided with the Samnites, such as the Aurunci, were crushed.</p></div>
